  "id": "behavioral-coping",
  "term": "behavioral coping",
  "definition": "Behavioral coping refers to the ways people respond to negative emotions caused by stressful events or public emergencies. In this source, it includes coping by focusing on different kinds of information, such as self-related information or information about the group, to help lessen emotions like fear, anxiety, or sadness.",
